Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `CoC_Number`: Used to derive a two–letter state code with `SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2)`.  
• `Unsheltered_Homeless`: Unsheltered homeless head‑count to be summed.  
• `Count_Year`: Filter the two target years (2015 and 2018).  
• (Optional) `CoC_Name`, `Overall_Homeless`, etc. – only for quick sanity‑checks / previews.  

Typical conditions  

• `Count_Year IN (2015,2018)` to restrict the time window.  
• `Unsheltered_Homeless IS NOT NULL` to ignore blank rows.  

Ten exploratory → production SQL samples
```sql
-- 1. Quick look at the distinct years in the table 
SELECT DISTINCT Count_Year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
ORDER BY Count_Year;
```

```sql
-- 2. Preview a handful of 2015 rows and key columns
SELECT CoC_Number, CoC_Name, Unsheltered_Homeless, Count_Year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
WHERE Count_Year = 2015
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Nation‑wide total unsheltered counts by year (sample)
SELECT Count_Year,
       SUM(Unsheltered_Homeless) AS nationwide_unsheltered
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
GROUP BY Count_Year
ORDER BY Count_Year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. State‑level unsheltered totals for 2015 (top 20 rows)
SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state,
       SUM(Unsheltered_Homeless) AS unsheltered_2015
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
WHERE Count_Year = 2015
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. State‑level unsheltered totals for 2018 (top 20 rows)
SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state,
       SUM(Unsheltered_Homeless) AS unsheltered_2018
FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
WHERE Count_Year = 2018
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Pivot both years side‑by‑side for each state (first 20)
SELECT
  state,
  SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) AS unsheltered_2015,
  SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2018 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) AS unsheltered_2018
FROM (
  SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state,
         Count_Year,
         Unsheltered_Homeless
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
  WHERE Count_Year IN (2015,2018)
)
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add percentage change 2015→2018 (top 20 rows)
SELECT
  state,
  unsheltered_2015,
  unsheltered_2018,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(unsheltered_2018 - unsheltered_2015, unsheltered_2015) AS pct_change
FROM (
  SELECT
    state,
    SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) AS unsheltered_2015,
    SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2018 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) AS unsheltered_2018
  FROM (
    SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state,
           Count_Year,
           Unsheltered_Homeless
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
    WHERE Count_Year IN (2015,2018)
  )
  GROUP BY state
)
ORDER BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. National average of state percentage changes
WITH state_pct AS (
  SELECT
    state,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2018 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) -
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END),
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END)) AS pct_change
  FROM (
    SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state, Count_Year, Unsheltered_Homeless
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
    WHERE Count_Year IN (2015,2018)
  )
  GROUP BY state
)
SELECT AVG(pct_change) AS national_avg_pct_change
FROM state_pct;
```

```sql
-- 9. State pct_change together with national average & distance (top 20)
WITH state_pct AS (
  SELECT
    state,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2018 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) -
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END),
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END)) AS pct_change
  FROM (
    SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state, Count_Year, Unsheltered_Homeless
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
    WHERE Count_Year IN (2015,2018)
  )
  GROUP BY state
),
nat_avg AS (SELECT AVG(pct_change) AS nat_avg FROM state_pct)
SELECT
  s.state,
  s.pct_change,
  n.nat_avg,
  ABS(s.pct_change - n.nat_avg) AS diff_from_avg
FROM state_pct s CROSS JOIN nat_avg n
ORDER BY diff_from_avg
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: five states whose pct_change is closest to the national average
WITH state_pct AS (
  SELECT
    state,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2018 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END) -
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END),
                SUM(CASE WHEN Count_Year = 2015 THEN Unsheltered_Homeless END)) AS pct_change
  FROM (
    SELECT SUBSTR(CoC_Number,1,2) AS state, Count_Year, Unsheltered_Homeless
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.sdoh_hud_pit_homelessness.hud_pit_by_coc`
    WHERE Count_Year IN (2015,2018)
  )
  GROUP BY state
),
nat_avg AS (SELECT AVG(pct_change) AS nat_avg FROM state_pct)
SELECT state
FROM (
  SELECT
    s.state,
    ABS(s.pct_change - n.nat_avg) AS diff_from_avg,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY ABS(s.pct_change - n.nat_avg)) AS rn
  FROM state_pct s CROSS JOIN nat_avg n
)
WHERE rn <= 5
ORDER BY rn;
```
These ten queries progress from simple inspection to the complete computation that returns the five state abbreviations whose 2015‑to‑2018 unsheltered homeless percentage change is closest to the national average of such changes.
